From 9d83812b2b62024ed06dcdd6c9b85f0d70088571 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: test <test@local>
Date: Sat, 23 May 2026 12:13:55 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 31/42] P09.69: CxxException via From<CxxRawError> (1.13 throws
 Phase 2A)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The MIR pass cxx_throws_wrap now auto-converts the catch
payload from CxxRawError (what the runtime helper produces)
to whatever Err type the user declared in their Result —
provided the type impls From<CxxRawError>.

User can now write:

    extern "C++" {
        #[rustc_cxx_throws]
        fn maybe_throws(x: i32) -> Result<i32, CxxException>;
    }

and the catch path automatically calls
`<CxxException as From<CxxRawError>>::from` on the raw
helper return before wrapping into Result::Err.

Smoke test confirms:

    maybe_throws(5)   →  Ok(10)                    ✅
    maybe_throws(-1)  →  Err(kind=Runtime)         ✅
                                  ^^^ from CxxException's
                                      typed-kind mapping

The MIR shape changes when conversion is needed. Without
conversion:

  bb_err_wrap:
    dest = Result::Err(move raw_err_local)
    goto orig_target

With conversion (E != CxxRawError):

  bb_err_convert:
    converted = <E as From<CxxRawError>>::from(move raw_err_local)
      -> [return: bb_err_finalize, unwind: Continue]
  bb_err_finalize:
    dest = Result::Err(move converted)
    goto orig_target

The CxxThrowsCleanup unwind action points at bb_err_convert
when conversion is required; codegen's catch BB still stores
the helper result into raw_err_local (typed as CxxRawError)
and branches to bb_err_convert, which then calls the user's
From impl and continues.

CxxRawError is looked up via
`rustc_diagnostic_item = "CxxRawError"`. The cxx runtime
crate marks its type with this attribute. If the diagnostic
item isn't in scope (no cxx crate dependency), the pass falls
back to the Phase 1 behavior — trust the user's declared
type. This keeps the Phase 1 smoke test (smoke.rs) working
unchanged.

If the conversion is required but `E: From<CxxRawError>`
doesn't hold, the pass emits a `span_delayed_bug` that
surfaces as a compile error rather than silently
miscompiling.

Resolution uses tcx.codegen_select_candidate against the
`From` lang item, then tcx.associated_items().find_by_*
to locate the `from` method, then ty::Instance::try_resolve
to monomorphize.

The conversion call's unwind action is Continue — if the
user's `From::from` panics, the panic propagates up the
stack like any other Rust panic. (`From` impls shouldn't
panic; this just matches normal Rust semantics.)

New diagnostic item symbol `CxxRawError` added in
rustc_span/src/symbol.rs.
